Hermes Desktop: start a chat in a chosen folder, and pick folders on Windows (drive list, typed absolute path).

Why: the Webapp's "Add folders as context" / working-directory picker opened at "/" on a Windows backend with no drive selector or editable path, and a
plugin could not start a chat in a given folder (host.newChat had no cwd), so project-bound chats needed the folder to be picked by hand.

What: (1) requestFreshSession/newSessionInProfile/newSessionInAgent take an optional folder that the next fresh draft starts in, exactly as picking it in
the composer would (explicit workspace target, so the backend records it as sessions.cwd); host.newChat(profile, { cwd }) passes it and
host.supportsNewChatCwd lets a plugin feature-detect. Nothing changes for callers that pass no folder. (2) The remote folder picker gets a typed absolute
path field (Enter to go), drive chips (drives found by listing each root; none on a POSIX backend) and a clear message for a relative path.

Applied after webapp-route-guard.patch and webapp-mcp-recovery.patch (it modifies the files the route guard patch added). Tests: remote-picker-paths.test.ts
(extended) and store/fresh-session-workspace.test.ts; tsc --noEmit clean for touched files. Upstream-able (hermes-agent apps/desktop).

